Suppose $G$ is a finite group, and let $A \subset G \times G$ be a subset of density $\alpha$. Are there $\gg_\alpha |G|^3$ triples $x, y, g$ such that $(x, y), (gx, y), (x, gy)$ all lie in $A$? \href{https://huggingface.co/datasets/ulamai/UnsolvedMath}{[S1]}

